# X05 portable character across two hosts (tests/smoke_net_join_portable_across_hosts.gd)
# main bcf46366c, stock Godot 4.7, one run at a time, isolated TB_NET_RUN_ID/--out.
run 1: 21/23. Two failures, both explained:
  - "personal progress travelled": FIXTURE ERROR. The first fixture used an undeclared
    flag id; character_save.gd saves only flags declared SCOPE_PLAYER in the
    progression_state.gd scope table, so it rightly stayed behind. The fixture now uses
    the declared player flag water_swim_lesson_briefed.
  - "the traveller never wrote a world file": OPEN, UNEXPLAINED, INTERMITTENT. The client
    wrote user://worlds/slot-0/world.json (empty world flags, created 06:02:09) and
    characters/<its boot character id>/character.json at the same second, ~8 s after
    leaving host A (portable file 06:02:01) while joined to host B. The world holds
    neither host's flags, so it is not a host world import. Run 2 instrumented
    Game.save_game(): never called on that peer, and the stray file did not appear.
    Remaining writers to check: ledger_rpc.gd save_world call sites, realm_shells.gd,
    water/stormwood direct save_world. Not reproduced in runs 2-4.
run 2: 22/23 (fixture error only; no stray world file).
run 3: 23/23 PASS   (x05-portable-across-hosts-run3.log)
run 4: 23/23 PASS   (x05-portable-across-hosts-run4.log)
Proves on loopback: same stable character id admitted by two different hosts; declared
personal progress restored from its own character file; each world's flags stay in that
world (no world import, host worlds untouched by the traveller); traveller writes only
its own character file.
